§ `Chapters 12 to 16 -- scutage, aid, summons and service`

§§ `Chapter 12 -- no scutage or aid without common counsel`

-- 12.1 names three occasions on which an aid needs no common counsel: ransoming "our person",
-- making "our eldest son a knight", and "once" marrying "our eldest daughter".  "Once" is read as
-- the first and only aid for that marriage, so the third occasion fails if an aid for the marriage
-- of the eldest daughter has been levied before.
-- src:31 | No scutage nor aid shall be imposed in our kingdom, unless by common counsel of our kingdom, except for ransoming our person, for making our eldest son a knight, and for once marrying our eldest daughter;
@ref Chapter 12 clause 12.1 (src:31)
GIVEN levy IS A LevyKind
      purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` IF
        levy EQUALS Aid
    AND (   purpose EQUALS `ransoming the person`
         OR purpose EQUALS `making the eldest son a knight`
         OR (   purpose EQUALS `once marrying the eldest daughter`
            AND (NOT `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before`)))

-- Chapter 14 puts "(except in the three cases aforesaid)" after "aid" and before "or of a
-- scutage", so the exception is read as reaching aids only: a scutage always needs common
-- counsel (fork F12).
-- src:31 | No scutage nor aid shall be imposed in our kingdom, unless by common counsel of our kingdom, except for ransoming our person, for making our eldest son a knight, and for once marrying our eldest daughter;
@ref Chapter 12 clause 12.1 (src:31)
GIVEN levy IS A LevyKind
      purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ch 12 -- the levy needs the common counsel of the kingdom` IF
    NOT (`ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` levy purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before`)

-- 12.2: for the three occasions "there shall not be levied more than a reasonable aid".
-- gloss (not the text's): whether an aid is "reasonable" is a judgment, taken as a plain input.
-- src:31 | No scutage nor aid shall be imposed in our kingdom, unless by common counsel of our kingdom, except for ransoming our person, for making our eldest son a knight, and for once marrying our eldest daughter;
-- src:31 | and for these there shall not be levied more than a reasonable aid.
@ref Chapter 12 clause 12.1-12.2 (src:31)
GIVEN levy IS A LevyKind
      purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` IS
    IF   (   `ch 12 -- the levy needs the common counsel of the kingdom` levy purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before`
         AND (NOT `it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom`))
      OR (   `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` levy purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before`
         AND (NOT `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid`))
    THEN Barred
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless by common counsel of our kingdom, except for" the three purposes, and "not ... more than a reasonable aid" (a limit the text states).
    ELSE `Not barred`

-- 12.3: "In like manner it shall be done concerning aids from the citizens of London."
-- src:31 | In like manner it shall be done concerning aids from the citizens of London.
@ref Chapter 12 clause 12.3 (src:31)
GIVEN purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 12 -- an aid from the citizens of London may be imposed` IS
    `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` `it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom` `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid`

§§ `Chapter 13 -- the liberties of London and of other towns`

-- src:33 | And the citizens of London shall have all their ancient liberties and free customs, as well by land as by water;
@ref Chapter 13 clause 13.1 (src:33)
GIVEN `they are the citizens of London` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 13 -- the citizens of London have all their ancient liberties and free customs, by land and by water` IS
    IF `they are the citizens of London`
    THEN Entitled
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`

-- src:33 | furthermore, we decree and grant that all other cities, boroughs, towns, and ports shall have all their liberties and free customs.
@ref Chapter 13 clause 13.2 (src:33)
GIVEN `it is a city, borough, town or port other than London` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 13 -- all other cities, boroughs, towns and ports have all their liberties and free customs` IS
    IF `it is a city, borough, town or port other than London`
    THEN Entitled
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`

§§ `Chapter 14 -- the summons for the common counsel`

-- The duty to summon arises when common counsel is needed; the days between summons and the
-- date fixed are tested in the next rule, because the text fixes no time for the summoning itself.
-- src:35 | And for obtaining the common counsel of the kingdom anent the assessing of an aid (except in the three cases aforesaid) or of a scutage, we will cause to be summoned the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls, and greater barons, by our letters under seal;
@ref Chapter 14 clause 14.1 (src:35)
GIVEN levy IS A LevyKind
      purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 14 -- the King will cause the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons to be summoned by letters under seal` IS
    IF `ch 12 -- the levy needs the common counsel of the kingdom` levy purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before`
    THEN PARTY `the King`
         MUST `cause the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons to be summoned by letters under seal`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 14: the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons were not summoned by letters under seal"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:35 | and we will moreover cause to be summoned generally, through our sheriffs and bailiffs, all others who hold of us in chief, for a fixed date, namely, after the expiry of at least forty days, and at a fixed place;
@ref Chapter 14 clause 14.2 (src:35)
GIVEN levy IS A LevyKind
      purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 14 -- the King will cause all others who hold of him in chief to be summoned generally` IS
    IF `ch 12 -- the levy needs the common counsel of the kingdom` levy purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before`
    THEN PARTY `the King`
         MUST `cause all others who hold of the King in chief to be summoned generally through the sheriffs and bailiffs, for a fixed date after at least forty days and at a fixed place`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 14: the other tenants in chief were not summoned generally through the sheriffs and bailiffs"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:35 | and in all letters of such summons we will specify the reason of the summons.
@ref Chapter 14 clause 14.3 (src:35)
GIVEN levy IS A LevyKind
      purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 14 -- the King will specify the reason of the summons in all letters of summons` IS
    IF `ch 12 -- the levy needs the common counsel of the kingdom` levy purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before`
    THEN PARTY `the King`
         MUST `specify the reason of the summons in all letters of summons`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 14: a letter of summons did not specify the reason of the summons"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- "after the expiry of at least forty days": the date fixed is at least forty days after the
-- summons is made (fork F14: forty elapsed days is taken to be enough).
-- src:35 | And for obtaining the common counsel of the kingdom anent the assessing of an aid (except in the three cases aforesaid) or of a scutage, we will cause to be summoned the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls, and greater barons, by our letters under seal;
-- src:35 | and we will moreover cause to be summoned generally, through our sheriffs and bailiffs, all others who hold of us in chief, for a fixed date, namely, after the expiry of at least forty days, and at a fixed place;
-- src:35 | and in all letters of such summons we will specify the reason of the summons.
@ref Chapter 14 clause 14.1-14.3 (src:35)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ch 14 -- the least number of days between the summons and the date fixed` MEANS 40

-- src:35 | And for obtaining the common counsel of the kingdom anent the assessing of an aid (except in the three cases aforesaid) or of a scutage, we will cause to be summoned the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls, and greater barons, by our letters under seal;
-- src:35 | and we will moreover cause to be summoned generally, through our sheriffs and bailiffs, all others who hold of us in chief, for a fixed date, namely, after the expiry of at least forty days, and at a fixed place;
-- src:35 | and in all letters of such summons we will specify the reason of the summons.
@ref Chapter 14 clause 14.1-14.3 (src:35)
GIVEN `the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons were summoned by letters under seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all other tenants in chief were summoned generally through the sheriffs and bailiffs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days between the summons and the date fixed` IS A NUMBER
      `a place was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every letter of summons specified the reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ch 14 -- the summons for the common counsel is as the Charter requires` IF
        `the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons were summoned by letters under seal`
    AND `all other tenants in chief were summoned generally through the sheriffs and bailiffs`
    AND `days between the summons and the date fixed` AT LEAST `ch 14 -- the least number of days between the summons and the date fixed`
    AND `a place was fixed`
    AND `every letter of summons specified the reason`

-- src:35 | And when the summons has thus been made, the business shall proceed on the day appointed, according to the counsel of such as are present, although not all who were summoned have come.
@ref Chapter 14 clause 14.4 (src:35)
GIVEN `the summons has been made as the Charter requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not all who were summoned have come` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `ch 14 -- the business proceeds on the day appointed according to the counsel of those present` IS
    IF `the summons has been made as the Charter requires`
    THEN Obliged
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Obligation not covered`

§§ `Chapter 15 -- aids taken by lords`

-- src:37 | We will not for the future grant to any one licence to take an aid from his own free tenants, except to ransom his body, to make his eldest son a knight, and once to marry his eldest daughter;
@ref Chapter 15 clause 15.1 (src:37)
GIVEN purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 15 -- the King may grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants` IS
    IF `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` Aid purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except to ransom his body, to make his eldest son a knight, and once to marry his eldest daughter".
    THEN `Not barred`
    ELSE Barred

-- src:37 | We will not for the future grant to any one licence to take an aid from his own free tenants, except to ransom his body, to make his eldest son a knight, and once to marry his eldest daughter;
@ref Chapter 15 clause 15.1 (src:37)
GIVEN purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 15 -- the King will not grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants, except for the three purposes` IS
    IF `ch 15 -- the King may grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants` purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` EQUALS Barred
    THEN PARTY `the King`
         SHANT `grant a licence to take an aid from his own free tenants`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 15: a licence was granted to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants for a purpose other than the three"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 15.2: "on each of these occasions there shall be levied only a reasonable aid" (no one is named).
-- src:37 | and on each of these occasions there shall be levied only a reasonable aid.
@ref Chapter 15 clause 15.2 (src:37)
GIVEN purpose IS AN AidPurpose
      `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 15 -- the aid levied by a lord on one of the three occasions may be this aid` IS
    IF `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` Aid purpose `an aid for the marriage of the eldest daughter has been levied before`
    THEN IF `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only a reasonable aid".
         THEN `Not barred`
         ELSE Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: only because "only" closes the amount of the aid (a reasonable aid); the branch is reached by a levy that is not an aid on one of the three occasions, which that sentence does not name).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 16 -- service for a knight's fee`

-- gloss (not the text's): the service demanded and the service due are stated in the same unit,
-- whatever the service is measured in.
-- src:39 | No one shall be compelled to perform greater service for a knight’s fee, or for any other free tenement, than is due therefrom.
@ref Chapter 16 (src:39)
GIVEN `the holding is a knight's fee or another free tenement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `service demanded` IS A NUMBER
      `service due from the holding` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 16 -- greater service than is due may be demanded` IS
    IF `the holding is a knight's fee or another free tenement`
    THEN IF `service demanded` GREATER THAN `service due from the holding`
         THEN Barred
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "greater service ... than is due therefrom" (a limit the text states).
         ELSE `Not barred`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`
